doc/scaffolding-and-import-boundaries:
scaffolding & import boundaries main  main injection leaf adapter library lifecycle hook mount package page product slice public surface seed slice shell slice slice app tier apps/main apps mount, wire, and inject. product logic lives in [[slice|slices]], never in the app shell. [[slice|slices]] are **[[seed slice|seed slices]]** `apps/main/slices/seed/<m>/`,  or **[[product slice|product slices]]** `apps/main/slices/product/<f>/` every [[slice]] is built the same way. **structure:** [[seed slice|seed slices]] and [[product slice|product slices]] are built identically: same api, web and mobile layers and patterns. every [[slice]] relates to the app the same way. **imports:** a slice imports only libs and packages. configs, slice infra (db), [[leaf adapter|leaf adapters]] (toast, i18n) and other assets are [[injection|injected]] by the app, only at the [[mount]] point. **exports:** the app imports only what a slice exposes through its [[public surface]]. **orchestration:** the app mounts slices and owns all wiring between them. slices emit [[lifecycle hook|lifecycle hooks]] with facts and intentions; the app decides what to do with them, potentially calling another slice's [[public surface]]. slices differ in one thing only: whether they may reach each other. a **[[seed slice]]** never reaches another seed slice — no deep imports, and no service calling another seed slice's service, not even through its [[public surface]]. only the app may call a seed slice's public surface. a seed slice carries no knowledge of its neighbours, which is what lets a different project take it. **[[product slice|product slices]]** may reach each other directly. a product slice exists only for this product, so it is a code-organization convention, not an import boundary. this architecture tries to achieve: consistency and decoupability. **consistency:** a developer working in any [[slice]] reads the same structure and the same patterns, no per-slice dialects, no relearning. **decoupability:** removing a seed slice should be simple: remove the seed slice, its [[mount]] and its wiring, and anything that still breaks is a declared need, breaking where it was declared. both properties come from the same boundaries: self-contained seed slices, injected dependencies, app-owned orchestration. the app–slice contract mod2 the app reaches a [[slice]] only through its barrels: `api/index.ts` · `web/index.ts` · `shared/index.ts` (the wire contract) · `api/models/index.ts` (db-client aggregation only). everything behind a barrel is internal — a deep import is a violation. at [[mount]], the app [[injection|injects]] what the slice declared it needs: configs, db, adapters, other slices' capabilities. the mount returns the slice's capabilities — services, hooks, components, routes. only the app holds them; another slice can declare a need, and the app decides whether to inject. mod1 mod3 wiring and plumbing live in the app: a slice emits [[lifecycle hook|lifecycle hooks]], the app listens and decides, potentially calling another slice's capability. a slice never listens to another slice directly. cfg2 env vars drive what mounts: which slices mount and which configs inject come from env vars, never hardcode. the pointer to which config is consumed lives outside the config object. configs.md mod7 a [[library]] never imports another library — libraries import node modules only. crossing the boundary — only an index crosses html ../assets/scaffolding-and-import-boundaries/crossing-the-boundary.html  where code lives imports are scoped by [[tier]]: `@configs/…` · `@libs/…` · `@modules/…` ([[seed slice|seed slices]]) · `@product/…` ([[product slice|product slices]]) · `@apps/…`. nothing imports `@apps/*`. platform belongs in the [[package]] name, never in the scope: `@libs/web-components`, `@libs/mobile-components`. scf8 scf11 every level has a `shared/` folder holding what its children consume: repo `shared/` ([[library|libs]] + [[seed slice|seed slices]], consumed by all apps) · `apps/main/slices/product/shared/` (shared by all product slices) · `<seed slice>/shared/` and `<product slice>/shared/` (across that [[slice]]'s [[slice app|slice apps]]). shared code sits at the nearest level above all its consumers — never in `lib` folders. placement ladder (first fit wins): pure data → `configs/` · generic engine → `shared/libs/` · reusable [[slice]] slice → `apps/main/slices/seed/` · this-product [[slice]] slice → `apps/main/slices/product/` · wiring → app shell. the repo tree — a shared/ at every scope, holding what its children consume ascii repo/
├── configs/          pure data · injected at mount
│
├── apps/
│   └── main/                     the product · own db
│       ├── shared/               the app shells
│       │   ├── api/          shell: mounts + wires
│       │   ├── web/          shell: mounts + wires
│       │   └── mobile/       shell: mounts + wires
│       └── slices/
│           ├── seed/                     ◀ product-agnostic · ships with the seed
│           │   └── <seed slice>/
│           │       ├── api/          ◀ slice app
│           │       ├── web/          ◀ slice app
│           │       ├── mobile/       ◀ slice app
│           │       └── shared/       ◀ shared across slice apps
│           └── product/                  ◀ product-specific
│               └── <product slice>/
│                   ├── api/          ◀ slice app
│                   ├── web/          ◀ slice app
│                   └── shared/       ◀ shared across slice apps
│
└── shared/           ◀ shared by the whole repo
    └── libs/          generic engines a ui capability — the member picker type-ahead over the users the current user may share with, resolving to a user id, or to an email address when that person has no account yet. it lives in `user-organization-mgmt` because uom is the only slice that knows users, memberships and org visibility — one declarer, and no product slice reimplements it. it reaches other slices by export: uom puts it on its web [[public surface]], and the app [[injection|injects]] it into the product slice that declared the need. where it lives — inside the slice that owns the knowledge apps/main/slices/seed/user-organization-mgmt/web/
├── components/members/memberpicker.tsx    the capability
└── index.ts                               the public surface how uom exports it — the barrel is the whole surface; nothing else is reachable // apps/main/slices/seed/user-organization-mgmt/web/index.ts
// public web surface — what a consuming app imports.

